= Client Entertainment and Hospitality

== Building Client Relationships with Integrity

At Noice & Toit LLP, cultivating enduring relationships with corporate clients, joint venture partners, and prospective talent is essential to our partnership's long-term success. Business hospitality, client lunches, and hosted dinners offer valuable opportunities to discuss strategic matters, review ongoing engagements, and celebrate milestone achievements in a relaxed, professional setting.

However, business entertainment carries heightened financial, reputational, and regulatory exposure. Client hospitality must always be purposeful, moderate, and fully transparent. It must never give the appearance of impropriety, conflict of interest, or inducement.

== Documenting Legitimate Business Purpose

Tax authorities and client procurement teams routinely scrutinize business entertainment deductions. To withstand audit scrutiny, every hosted event or client dinner claimed on an expense report must be substantiated with comprehensive documentation.

#card-do("Document the business objective and attendee roster")[
  Every hosted meal or client entertainment submission must include:
  - The specific business agenda, transaction, or client matter discussed.
  - A complete roster of all attendees, including full names, company affiliations, and official corporate titles.
  - An itemized merchant bill showing all food and beverage charges.
]

#card-dont("Submit vague or undocumented entertainment claims")[
  Never submit claims with generic notes such as "dinner with contacts" or "business lunch". Reports lacking verified attendee names and clear corporate affiliations will be rejected by Finance.
]

== The Decision Framework for Hospitality and Alcohol

Unlike individual solo travel, where all alcohol is strictly non-reimbursable, corporate hospitality involves more nuanced considerations regarding group composition, milestone celebrations, and beverage allowances.

Rather than providing fragmented written descriptions that lead to ambiguity and audit disputes, Noice & Toit LLP centralizes all rules governing group dining, team celebrations, attendee ratios, alcohol allowances, and late-night expenditures into a single, authoritative visual decision matrix.

#card-do("Consult the visual matrix before hosting")[
  All spending limits, required internal-to-external attendee ratios, allowable alcohol percentages, and late-night expenditure cutoffs are established exclusively in Figure 2: Dining and Entertainment Decision Matrix in Chapter 13.
]

#card-dont("Rely on assumptions or verbal manager promises")[
  Do not assume that casual verbal approval from a colleague overrides the formal visual standards. If a hospitality claim violates the thresholds set out in Figure 2, Finance will reduce the reimbursement or disallow the claim entirely.
]

== Entertainment Venues, Sports, and Cultural Events

Client entertainment should generally take place at professional dining establishments, private dining rooms, or business clubs. Entertaining at other types of venues requires additional caution:

=== Sporting Events and Theater Performances
Taking clients to theater performances, symphony concerts, golf tournaments, or professional sporting matches is permissible only when structured around an active business discussion:
- The host employee must attend the event alongside the client; sending client tickets without firm representation is treated as a gift and must follow our central Gift & Hospitality Policy.
- Tickets must be purchased in standard seating tiers; luxury suites, VIP hospitality boxes, and backstage passes require prior written authorization from the Managing Partner.

=== Prohibited Entertainment Venues
Under no circumstances may firm funds be expended at night clubs, gentleman's clubs, casinos, or venues that conflict with our professional standards and inclusive workplace culture. Any expense incurred at such establishments will be rejected in full and referred to the Ethics and Conduct Committee.

== Internal Team Celebrations and Project Milestones

Recognizing team dedication following the closing of an intense transaction, litigation verdict, or year-end milestone is encouraged:
- Internal team dinners require advance budget approval from your Department Director.
- The celebration must be tied to a documented project milestone or quarterly team review.
- Compliance with the internal dining parameters illustrated in Figure 2 (Chapter 13) is mandatory.

== Frequently Asked Questions

*Q: What if a client insists on ordering an unusually expensive vintage wine?*\
A: While we aim to be gracious hosts, employees should guide wine selections toward quality standard business bottles. Review the beverage caps in Figure 2 (Chapter 13). If a client dinner significantly exceeds the visual matrix threshold, the excess alcohol amount must be deducted or approved by an Equity Partner.

*Q: Can I expense coffee or light snacks when meeting a prospective hire?*\
A: Yes. Casual recruiting discussions at coffee shops are allowable when connected to active job requisitions. Note the candidate name and target role in the report comments.
